From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: SBS: Report the relative state of charge as
 capacity

The driver reports AbsoluteStateOfCharge (0x0e) as capacity. The Smart
Battery specification defines it relative to DesignCapacity, while the
power supply ABI defines capacity as the fraction of a full battery,
which is RelativeStateOfCharge (0x0d), relative to FullChargeCapacity.

On a worn battery the two differ by the capacity loss. A MacBookPro15,1
reported 87 percent at a relative state of charge of 98 percent.

Read RelativeStateOfCharge instead.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
--- a/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
@@ -322,7 +322,7 @@
 	{0x0b, SMBUS_READ_WORD, offsetof(struct acpi_battery, rate_avg)},
 	{0x0f, SMBUS_READ_WORD, offsetof(struct acpi_battery, capacity_now)},
 	{0x10, SMBUS_READ_WORD, offsetof(struct acpi_battery, full_charge_capacity)},
-	{0x0e, SMBUS_READ_WORD, offsetof(struct acpi_battery, state_of_charge)},
+	{0x0d, SMBUS_READ_WORD, offsetof(struct acpi_battery, state_of_charge)},
 	{0x17, SMBUS_READ_WORD, offsetof(struct acpi_battery, cycle_count)},
 	{0x16, SMBUS_READ_WORD, offsetof(struct acpi_battery, state)},
 };
